    "title": "Manhattan City Commissioners discuss design options for Moro Street in Aggieville - NewsBreak",
    "text": "3 hours ago The City Commission reviewed conceptual options for the future reconstruction of Moro Street in Aggieville from 11th Street to N. Manhattan Ave. this week. Four refined concepts were provided within the 60-foot right-of-way between storefronts on Moro that generally feature angled parking on one side of the street, a 20-foot driving lane, and the potential for mid-block pedestrian crossings and other landscaping and pedestrian amenities. Read full article\nRead in NewsBreak",
